    "limitations": "Model covers only syngas side between BFD 8 and 9; no utility/steam side, no fouling, no heat loss, no condensation kinetics. Outlet state SYNGAS_TO_SHIFT from DWSIM under these assumed setpoints: T 349.9 C (350 C before valve), P 27.8 bar, vapour fraction 1.0, total 240967 kg/h conserved, components kg/h: Methane 12873.3, CO 78313.2, CO2 10654.8, H2 18140.5, H2O 119344.4, N2 1640.8. Net cooling duty (enthalpy removed) 100749 kW for 871->350 C at given flow; at 28.3 bar no water condensation occurs at this assumed outlet (vapour fraction 1.0). If actual plant shift inlet temperature or pressure drop differs, temperature, pressure and duty will differ proportionally. This run does NOT reproduce or validate any withheld Exhibit 3-17 stream-table values for stream 9; it is a forward calculation from the supplied inlet with stated assumptions only. Property package PR is an approximation; at 871 C ideal-gas enthalpy dominates, but real-gas effects and water association introduce uncertainty."
